summary: Verify ACPI is enabled
description: |
    Verify that ACPI is enabled at boot.  This is a sanity check for aarch64
    (64-bit ARM) servers which can use either ACPI or DeviceTree, and RHEL does
    not support DeviceTree, so a failure here indicates a firmware problem
    with the server.
contact: Jeffrey Bastian <jbastian@redhat.com>
component:
  - kernel
test: ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
adjust:
  - enabled: false
    when: arch != aarch64
duration: 15m
extra-summary: /kernel/acpi/enabled
extra-task: /kernel/acpi/enabled
